'RUN-TIME-ERROR
' Text that is not a number is an error naming the text, not a zero.
' The text arrives through MIRROR_TEXT, so this really is a run: TO_INTEGER is @BubasMemoizable and
' a literal would be refused while compiling. See constant/static-function-refuses.bu.
' ERROR: is not an INTEGER
' LINE: 9
PROGRAM P
    DECLARE n INTEGER
    n = TO_INTEGER(MIRROR_TEXT("twelve"))
    ASSERT "unreachable", n = 0
END.
